  "kind": "skill",
  "name": "Primer Design",
  "summary": "Designs and audits PCR and RT-qPCR primers with Primer3, explicit thermodynamic conditions, reference-based off-target amplification searches, and traceable sequence coordinates. Use for designing primer pairs, checking existing primers, exon-junction or isoform-specific assays, variant masking, cloning tails, multiplex compatibility, and interpreting Primer-BLAST results. Includes bounded local in-silico PCR and BLAST screening; distinguishes computational candidates from experimentally validated assays.",
